New Rock is a subdialect of the Rock language, a simple C-like language
compiling down to Pebble. New rock adds many extra featues, but it
mainly adds proper Pebble addressing support to the language to allow
all of the advanced concepts that can be expressed by Pebble AAE to also
be expressed by the Rock language. This does mean New Rock removed the
older Rock marker symbols, meaning code written in Rock will not compile
with a New Rock compiler.

The New Rock compiler can be found in the rockc/ folder relative to here
and can be compiled simply with

	cc -o bin/rockc newrock/rockc/*.c

from the current directory to generate one rockc binary. Running this 
without arguments should tell you how to use it.

(keep in mind, the current directory is assumed to be the root of the
indev tree)

rockpkg is a small pkgsrc-like package manager and build system for
the New Rock language. It reads .rockpkg build configuration files
which are used to fetch New Rock source code from the web, compile
the source code, and install the binary onto the system. The first
argument is to be the operation to perform, currently only 'install',
and the second is to be the path to the .rockpkg file to read. A
repository of New Rock build scripts can be found at

	http://pebblevm.org/rockpkg/

this is further sorted into <group>/<name>.rockpkg, eg. if I wanted to
install the program 'demos/one', I could fetch

	http://pebblevm.org/rockpkg/demos/basic.rockpkg

and install it using the rockpkg package manager

The package manager can be built by running

	cc -o bin/rockpkg newrock/rockpkg/*.c $(curl-config --libs)

from the current directory.
